  <div class="page-shell about__grid">
    <div>
      <p class="section__label">About</p>
      <h2 class="section__title" id="about-title">Systems meet stories</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="about__copy">
      <p>
        I work where technology, ethics, and imagination overlap — as a designer
        and philosopher focused on AI fairness, transparency, data ethics, and
        societal impact.
      </p>
      <p>
        At CERN I developed open resources and workshops on ethical futures; with
        Relatronica I run an experimental lab that uses speculative and critical
        design to open public debate on human–machine relations.
      </p>
      <p>
        Sound is part of the same inquiry: instruments, production, and field
        recording as ways to probe how humans and machines listen to — and shape
        — each other.
      </p>
      <p>
        Free software is not a side note: open, auditable systems are a
        precondition for accountable AI. I collaborate with research labs,
        cultural institutions, and communities that want responsibility designed
        in — not bolted on.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

